# the record of the class declares a toJSON: no guard answers for that name, and no look at the object shows that it is not found. What holds such an object is not written whole
# class P { constructor(v) { this.x = v; }  toJSON() { return 0; } }  JSON.stringify({ inner: new P("a") });
